      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T05:14:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Although I don\u0027t get the feedback from bluetooth team yet, I have traced the code by myself. And I do think this could happen. BluetoothAdapter#isEnabled() could not guarantee the onServiceConnected is fired.\n\nHere is the flow:\n1. When bluetooth service is up. The AdapterState (state machine) would transit to STATE_ON and callback to BluetoothManagerService\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/btservice/AdapterState.java;l\u003d162?q\u003dupdateAdapterState\u0026ss\u003dpiper%2FGoogle%2Faosp-master:packages%2Fmodules%2FBluetooth%2F\n2. The callback would send the message to handler thread of BluetoothManagerService and callback to all of the BluetoothProfileConnector\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/BluetoothManagerService.java?q\u003dbluetoothmanagerservice\n3. Then the BluetoothProfileConnector (which hold by BluetoothPan) would bind to pan service. If the bind successful, the onServiceConnected would call.\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/frameworks/base/core/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothProfileConnector.java;l\u003d53\n\nIn step 1, once AdapterState is STATE_ON, BluetoothAdapter#isEnabled() would return true. Since the step 2 send the message to handler thread, this means the whole flow is not synchronized. This could have race that BluetoothAdapter#isEnabled() is true but onServiceConnected is not called yet.",
      "parentUuid": "33ce9337_93ecd23f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 283,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 283,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "2a0e81c6a27de8c160385d8eb5acbafe623224e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
