      "writtenOn": "2021-12-14T10:10:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you don\u0027t do something like:\n\n    if (this !\u003d mBluetoothPanListener) return;\n\nhere, then the following can happen.\n\n1. onServiceConnected is called. Everything is good.\n2. The service crashes. onServiceDisconnected is called. The disconnect lambda gets posted to the handler thread but the handler thread is blocked for whatever reason.\n3. onServiceConnected is called. The connect lambda gets posted to the handler thread.\n4. mBluetoothPan gets reinitialized to non-null.\n\n\nNow we have a bug because mBluetoothPan is non-null but the listener is null, and future calls to onServiceDisconnected will have no effect.\n\n\nIn general I\u0027d advise reducing the amount of state in this code, for example, by making mBluetoothPan permanently non-null, and, if possible keeping the same listener object all the time. In general, the KISS principle applies.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 762,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 762,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "2a0e81c6a27de8c160385d8eb5acbafe623224e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
